cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal,
  work-in-progress synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI
  assistant by Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "reader-ergonomics-review (work in progress)"
abstract: >-
  The literature review as a genre of the reader-ergonomics family: the five steps, the files of a review (frame, protocol, sources, review, against, state of the art, position, baseline, references), the grey scoring, the second rater and the flow, as shapes with examples and checks. Scope only; the shapes are not yet written.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/reader-ergonomics-review"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - literature review
  - multivocal literature review
  - grey literature
  - snowballing
  - systematic review
  - reader-ergonomics
